From 2dae899b5657bc52b3d5b034f06d49b4ead6dd1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "@dev/8" <dev-8@main.hh.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:04:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sdk): an unlist drops the row and keeps the provider
 conversation (#37603)

A fleet seat moving off a host needs its row gone from the catalogue while
the backend keeps the transcript the next host resumes. Disposing did both
halves, so the only way to drop a row was to destroy the conversation.

`disposeSession` takes `preserveProviderSession: true`: the same disposal,
minus the two steps that ask a backend to delete - `deleted()` and each
chat's `disposeProviderChat()` - with the close reason `stopping` for a
nested backend. It answers `{provider, providerSessionId, directory?,
chatsRemoved}` so the caller keeps the resume id, and refuses with
`SessionNotFound`, `session-live` (a running turn, named), `stop-unproven`
(a session still held here) or a mismatched `expectProviderSessionId`,
all before anything is dropped. Plain disposal is unchanged.

Durability needs one thing a row cannot hold: the backend still lists the
conversation, so merging it back in on the next listing resurrects the
session the caller asked to be rid of - including after a restart, and with
`showExternalSessions` on. `SessionStore.unlisted` is that mark, kept in
`unlisted.json` beside the rows (which `forget` drops) and consulted by the
listing and by `loadUnlisted`; a session made again on the answered id
clears it.

Tests: red first on bc4c35c4e (6 of 7 fail there), and the durability case
is only green with the mark - a second store over the same folder, external
sessions shown, backend still listing the id.

Refs: @i/30-layers/32350-new-architecture-ahp-ade/32986-move-fleet-onto-ahpd/37603-ahpd-durable-unlist-primitive
